      "chunk_id": null,
      "contains_speech": true,
      "content": "Thanks, Isabella—I found your account and your recent order.\n\n### Where to find your order ID\nYou can usually find it in your **order confirmation email** (subject like “Your order is confirmed”) or on your account’s **Order History** page.  \nFor you, I see the recent order as: **#W4923227**.\n\n### Gift card balance\nYour gift card on file is **gift_card_8245350**, and the current balance is **$60.00**.\n\n### What payment you used for this order\nOrder **#W4923227** is **pending** and was paid with **credit card ending in 4336 (Mastercard)** for **$321.18**.\n\n### Can we switch this order to use your gift card?\nBecause the order total is **$321.18** and your gift card balance is **$60.00**, the gift card alone would not cover the order total. Also, for payment changes I can only switch to **one** alternate payment method for the order.\n\n**So:**\n- Switching to **gift card** would require enough balance to cover the order total/required amount.\n- Otherwise, we can switch the payment to your **Visa**.\n\n### Next step (need your confirmation)\nIf you still want me to proceed, please reply **yes** to confirm one of these options:\n\n1) **Switch payment to Visa** (credit card brand **visa**, last four **8902**) for order **#W4923227**  \n**OR**\n2) **Try switching to gift card** (gift card balance is $60.00)—I’ll proceed with the system’s allowed change, but it may fail due to insufficient balance.\n\nWhich option do you want, and should I proceed?",
